{
  "file": "legal-privacy.zh-CN.cliff",
  "stratum": "legal",
  "notes": "Quillmark consent portal: a privacy notice, the data processing agreement that goes with it and the abstract of a conference paper, written for CLARION-Core v0.3. Every item is labelled A to D in the first position of its tags. A decisive (the source alone cannot be translated correctly: the defined-term policy, the legal force of shall, must, may and may not, the entity names that stay in Latin script, or the chapter context that decides between two legitimate readings of one sentence). B high-risk (systematic model bias: date order, grouped digits and rounding, ICU plural and select payloads, enumerated item markers, all-capital typography). C cross-entry (a term or a clause number that only resolves against another entry of this file: the definitions section, the retention clause numbered 4.2 and the audit clause numbered 6.1). D normal text (ordinary clause prose and the abstract, kept as the baseline). Two minimal pairs share a source and a neutral id and differ on exactly one field, the context: clause-07a and clause-07b place the same purpose clause in the authorisation chapter and in the restriction chapter, and clause-09a and clause-09b place the same execution clause in those two chapters. Neither pair is decided by the standard header, which stays silent on both distinctions.",
  "provenance": {
    "source": "original text written for CLARION",
    "url": "",
    "license": "CC0-1.0",
    "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
    "redistributable": true,
    "human_verified": false,
    "verifier": "",
    "retrieved": "2026-01-01",
    "origin": "original",
    "context_origin": "original",
    "notes": "Original text written for this benchmark, therefore free of training-data contamination. The company, the portal, the agreement and the conference paper are invented and share nothing with the Ledgerline file in the same stratum."
  },
